# PR-1: PR-1: Customer onboarding and KYC identity verification

**Story.** As a prospective bank customer, I want to register my identity details so that a compliance officer can verify my eligibility and allow me to open an account, while ensuring underage users, self-verifications, and unverified account openings are blocked and my personal data remains protected.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] RegisterCustomerRequest requires non-empty FullName, Email, NationalId, and DateOfBirth; empty or whitespace string fields throw ArgumentException.
- [ ] POST api/customers (authorized with Policies.Customer) registers the currently signed-in user using ICurrentUser.UserId as Customer.Id, ignoring any external user identifier, sets Status to KycStatus.Pending, sets RegisteredAt to IClock.UtcNow, persists to BankDbContext.Customers, and publishes CustomerRegistered(CustomerId, OccurredAt).
- [ ] If a Customer record already exists for ICurrentUser.UserId, ICustomerService.RegisterAsync throws InvalidOperationException.
- [ ] If the applicant is under 18 years old as of the date derived from IClock.UtcNow (including one day before their 18th birthday, whereas exactly 18 years old is accepted), ICustomerService.RegisterAsync throws ArgumentException.
- [ ] GET api/customers/me (authorized with Policies.Customer) returns the signed-in user's Customer record via ICustomerService.GetAsync or 404 Not Found if not registered.
- [ ] POST api/customers/{id}/verify and POST api/customers/{id}/reject (authorized with Policies.Compliance) invoke VerifyAsync and RejectAsync respectively; if the caller is not in the Compliance role or if ICurrentUser.UserId equals customerId (self-verification or self-rejection), they throw UnauthorizedAccessException.
- [ ] VerifyAsync and RejectAsync throw KeyNotFoundException when customerId does not exist in BankDbContext.Customers.
- [ ] Customer.Verify(officerId) and Customer.Reject(officerId) transition Status from KycStatus.Pending to KycStatus.Verified or KycStatus.Rejected, set DecidedBy to officerId, and publish CustomerVerified or CustomerRejected; calling either method when Status is not Pending throws InvalidOperationException.
- [ ] KycAccountOpeningRule implements IAccountOpeningRule and throws UnauthorizedAccessException if the customer is unknown or Customer.Status is not KycStatus.Verified.
- [ ] CustomersModule registers ICustomerService and KycAccountOpeningRule as IAccountOpeningRule in DI, and Program.cs registers CustomersModule while BankDbContext exposes DbSet<Customer> Customers.
- [ ] Customer.NationalId and Customer.DateOfBirth are annotated with [Pii], and neither NationalId nor DateOfBirth ever appears in domain events (CustomerRegistered, CustomerVerified, CustomerRejected), application logs, or exception/error messages.

## Out of scope
- Updating customer profile fields or re-submitting a registration after rejection.
- Listing, searching, or filtering pending KYC applications for compliance officers.
- External identity provider, sanctions/PEP screening, or document upload integrations.
- Automated email or SMS notifications on registration, verification, or rejection.
- Account creation endpoints, balance management, or any monetary fees/ledger postings (no money movement occurs in this PR).

## Risks
- Self-verification or privilege escalation if compliance role checks or caller-vs-target UserId comparisons are omitted or if user identifiers are accepted from request payloads.
- Regulatory breach from onboarding minors if age calculation uses system clock instead of IClock.UtcNow or mishandles leap-year birthdays (e.g., February 29).
- GDPR/privacy violation if NationalId or DateOfBirth leaks into domain events, exception messages, or HTTP/application logs.
- Unverified or rejected customers opening bank accounts if KycAccountOpeningRule is not wired as IAccountOpeningRule or fails open on missing customer records.
- Invalid KYC state transitions (such as verifying a previously rejected customer) if Customer.Status is not enforced via a private setter and domain guard methods.

## Public contract
```
