# PR-7: PR-7: Loans application and four-eyes approval with disbursement

**Story.** As a verified customer, I want to apply for a fixed-rate loan paid into one of my own accounts and track its status, and as a loan officer, I want to approve or reject another customer's submitted loan so that funds are disbursed safely under four-eyes control.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] Implement the Loans module under src/Bank.Api/Modules/Loans/ following the agreed namespaces (Bank.Modules.Loans.Domain, Bank.Modules.Loans.Application, Bank.Modules.Loans.Api), register it via LoansModule in Program.cs, and add DbSet<Loan> Loans to BankDbContext.
- [ ] Loan domain entity in Bank.Modules.Loans.Domain has Id, CustomerId, DisbursementAccountId, Principal, TermMonths, AnnualRatePercent, MonthlyPayment, Status (with a private setter defaulting to LoanStatus.Submitted and transitioning only via entity methods), DecidedBy, DecisionNote, and AppliedAt, plus a public parameterless constructor and domain events LoanSubmitted, LoanApproved, and LoanRejected implementing IDomainEvent.
- [ ] POST api/loans (authorized with Policies.Customer) calls ILoanService.ApplyAsync using ICurrentUser.UserId as CustomerId (never from request body) and IClock.UtcNow as AppliedAt.
- [ ] ApplyAsync validates Principal is between 1000 and 50000 inclusive and TermMonths is between 6 and 120 inclusive, throwing ArgumentException if out of range.
- [ ] ApplyAsync verifies via IAccountService that DisbursementAccountId is owned by the calling customer, throwing UnauthorizedAccessException if not owned by the caller.
- [ ] ApplyAsync sets AnnualRatePercent to 5.5 and computes MonthlyPayment using the standard annuity formula P * r / (1 - (1 + r)^(-n)) where r = 0.055 / 12 and n = TermMonths, rounded to 2 decimal places using Math.Round(value, 2, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero).
- [ ] ApplyAsync persists the Loan with LoanStatus.Submitted and publishes LoanSubmitted(Loan.Id, Loan.CustomerId, Loan.Principal, AppliedAt) via IEventBus.
- [ ] GET api/loans/{id} (authorized with Policies.Customer) calls ILoanService.GetAsync, throwing KeyNotFoundException when the loan does not exist and UnauthorizedAccessException when the caller is neither the loan's CustomerId nor in Roles.LoanOfficer.
- [ ] POST api/loans/{id}/approve and POST api/loans/{id}/reject (authorized with Policies.LoanOfficer) call ILoanService.ApproveAsync and ILoanService.RejectAsync respectively.
- [ ] Both ApproveAsync and RejectAsync throw UnauthorizedAccessException if the caller is not in Roles.LoanOfficer or if the caller's UserId equals the loan's CustomerId (four-eyes rule), KeyNotFoundException if the loan is not found, and InvalidOperationException if Loan.Status is not LoanStatus.Submitted.
- [ ] RejectAsync throws ArgumentException if reason is null, empty, or whitespace, transitions Status to LoanStatus.Rejected, records DecidedBy and DecisionNote, persists the change, and publishes LoanRejected(Loan.Id, clock.UtcNow).
- [ ] ApproveAsync transitions Status to LoanStatus.Disbursed, records DecidedBy and optional DecisionNote, resolves the disbursement account's currency via IAccountService.GetAsync, and transfers Loan.Principal from BankAccounts.For(BankAccountKind.LoanFunding, currency) to Loan.DisbursementAccountId via ILedger.PostTransferAsync without modifying Account.Balance directly.
- [ ] ApproveAsync publishes LoanApproved(Loan.Id, Loan.CustomerId, Loan.Principal, clock.UtcNow) via IEventBus and notifies the customer via INotifier with a message containing no personal data (no PII).

## Out of scope
- Loan repayment schedules, installment billing, manual repayments, or automatic debit collection.
- Early loan payoff, refinancing, variable interest rates, fee charges, or external credit-scoring checks.
- Listing or filtering multiple loans endpoint (GET api/loans) beyond GET api/loans/{id}.
- Sending customer notifications upon loan rejection.
- Cross-currency FX conversion during loan disbursement (disbursement uses the target account's currency only).
- Adding any new NuGet packages or modifying Account.Balance directly.

## Risks
- Four-eyes control bypass if the loan officer identity check trusts client-supplied identifiers instead of ICurrentUser.UserId.
- Double disbursement or inconsistent loan state if concurrent approval requests succeed before status updates or if Loan becomes Disbursed when ILedger.PostTransferAsync fails.
- Incorrect monthly payment calculations caused by integer division, wrong monthly rate conversion, floating-point drift, or wrong rounding mode instead of MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero.
- Disbursement failure or wrong currency movement if LoanFunding account lookup does not match the disbursement account's currency.
- PII exposure in INotifier messages, logs, or domain events if customer names or account details are included.
- HTTP policy mismatch on GET api/loans/{id} potentially blocking loan officers who do not also hold the Customer policy claim unless policy configuration covers them.

## Public contract
```
