# PR-10: PR-10: Extract shared MoneyMath.ToCents helper and adopt across Fx, Fees, Deposits, and Loans

**Story.** As a Nordbank developer, I want a single shared MoneyMath.ToCents helper in Bank.Shared.Money used across the Fx, Fees, Deposits, and Loans modules so that all cent-rounding follows one consistent rule without changing any monetary amounts seen by customers.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] Create public static class MoneyMath in namespace Bank.Shared.Money (in its own file, no new NuGet packages) exposing public static decimal ToCents(decimal amount) implemented with Math.Round(amount, 2, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero).
- [ ] Unit tests for MoneyMath.ToCents verify exact decimal outputs: 2.345m returns 2.35m, -2.345m returns -2.35m, 2.344m returns 2.34m, -2.344m returns -2.34m, 10.00m returns 10.00m, and 0m returns 0m.
- [ ] Replace all duplicated cent-rounding logic in the Fx, Fees, Deposits, and Loans modules with calls to MoneyMath.ToCents(decimal), leaving zero inline Math.Round(..., 2, ...) calls in those four modules.
- [ ] Preserve exact monetary behavior across Fx, Fees, Deposits, and Loans: for all existing test cases and boundary inputs (including half-cent values such as 2.345m and -2.345m), every calculated conversion, fee, deposit interest, and loan payment amount equals the pre-refactor amount to the exact cent, and all amounts passed to ILedger.PostTransferAsync remain rounded to 2 decimal places.
- [ ] Preserve all existing endpoint authorization policies ([Authorize(Policy = ...)] for Customer, Staff, LoanOfficer, Compliance, Admin), role checks, and HTTP error responses (such as 401/403 for unauthorized callers and 400 for invalid amounts) in Fx, Fees, Deposits, and Loans.

## Out of scope
- Changing the rounding strategy away from 2 decimal places with MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero or altering any customer-facing fee, FX, interest, or loan amounts.
- Introducing a Money value object, currency-specific decimal precision (e.g. 0 or 3 decimals), currency formatting, or additional MoneyMath methods beyond ToCents(decimal).
- Refactoring rounding logic in any module outside Fx, Fees, Deposits, and Loans.
- Modifying API endpoints, DTOs, database schemas, authorization policies, or adding NuGet packages.

## Risks
- If any existing module used default MidpointRounding.ToEven or truncation instead of AwayFromZero, switching to MoneyMath.ToCents would alter customer amounts on half-cent boundaries (e.g., 2.345 -> 2.35 instead of 2.34), breaking the zero-behavior-change guarantee.
- Missing a rounding call site or accidentally changing whether rounding occurs on intermediate vs. final amounts in Fx, Fees, Deposits, or Loans could cause 1-cent discrepancies, customer over/under-charging, or ledger transfer imbalances.
- Passing unrounded sub-cent decimal values into ILedger.PostTransferAsync if a rounding call is inadvertently removed during refactoring.
- Using float or double intermediates before calling MoneyMath.ToCents could introduce binary floating-point rounding errors.

## Public contract
```
namespace Bank.Shared.Money:
  static class MoneyMath { static decimal ToCents(decimal amount); }   // rounds to 2 decimals, half away from zero (2.345 -> 2.35, -2.345 -> -2.35)
```

## Allowed scope
- `src/Bank.Api/Shared/Money/**`
- `src/Bank.Api/Modules/Fx/**`
- `src/Bank.Api/Modules/Fees/**`
- `src/Bank.Api/Modules/Deposits/**`
- `src/Bank.Api/Modules/Loans/**`

_Brief from the product owner:_ Rounding to cents is written separately in several modules. Create one shared helper and use it in the Fx, Fees, Deposits and Loans modules. This is a refactor: no customer may see a different amount afterwards.


ALLOWED SCOPE (glob): ['src/Bank.Api/Shared/Money/**', 'src/Bank.Api/Modules/Fx/**', 'src/Bank.Api/Modules/Fees/**', 'src/Bank.Api/Modules/Deposits/**', 'src/Bank.Api/Modules/Loans/**']

CODING CONVENTIONS:
# Coding conventions for Nordbank (the Builder must follow these)

Stack: C# / ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET 8+), EF Core (SQLite), xUnit. No new NuGet packages.

## Layout — one folder per module, one folder per layer
src/Bank.Api/Modules/<Module>/
  Api/          controllers + DTOs            (HTTP layer)
  Application/  services + interfaces         (use cases)
  Domain/       entities, enums, events       (business rules)
  Data/         repositories (optional)       (database access)
  <Module>Module.cs   static class with AddXModule(this IServiceCollection): services.AddScoped<IThing, Thing>()
Register a new module in Program.cs above the "// MODULES:" line.
Add a new table as a DbSet in src/Bank.Api/Data/BankDbContext.cs above the "// TABLES:" line.
Each module already has a CONSTITUTION.md written by the humans who own it: follow its rules.

## Rules
- Namespaces follow folders: Bank.Modules.<Module>.<Layer>.
- Controllers: [ApiController], [Route("api/...")], and ALWAYS an [Authorize(Policy = Policies.X)] (Bank.Modules.Auth.Policies:
  Customer, Staff, LoanOfficer, Compliance, Admin). Roles are in Bank.Modules.Auth.Roles.
- Current user: inject Bank.Modules.Auth.Application.ICurrentUser (UserId, IsInRole). Never trust user ids from request bodies.
- Time: inject Bank.Shared.Time.IClock and use clock.UtcNow. Never call DateTime.Now / DateTimeOffset.UtcNow directly.
- Settings: inject Bank.Shared.Settings.BankSettings (DefaultCurrency, SupportedCurrencies, DailyTransferLimit).
- Money: decimal only. Round to cents with Math.Round(x, 2, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero).
- Money moves ONLY through Bank.Modules.Ledger.Application.ILedger.PostTransferAsync(from, to, amount, reference),
  which returns the transfer id and works in ONE currency. The bank's own accounts:
  Bank.Modules.Ledger.Domain.BankAccounts.For(BankAccountKind.X, currency) with kinds
  LoanFunding, FeeIncome, FxClearing, DepositHolding, InterestExpense, Suspense (EUR, SEK, USD).
- Accounts: Bank.Modules.Accounts.Application.IAccountService (GetAsync, IsOwnerAsync, ForOwnerAsync). Never edit Account.Balance.
- State machines: an entity owns its status (private setter) and changes it only through methods that check the current state.
- Entities: public parameterless constructor and public settable properties (except a status with a private setter),
  so the database and tests can create them.
- Events: sealed records implementing Bank.Shared.Events.IDomainEvent (with DateTimeOffset OccurredAt), published with
  IEventBus.PublishAsync(...). Handlers implement IEventHandler<TEvent> and are registered in their module.
- Personal data properties get [Pii] (Bank.Shared). Never put personal data in events, logs or messages.
- Do not name a type "Ledger" outside the Ledger module (namespace clash).
- Keep files small; one public type per file unless they are tiny records.


