REQUIREMENT (issue):
# PR-12: PR-12: Hold large payments to new payees for compliance review

**Story.** As a compliance officer, I want payments of 5,000 EUR or more (EUR equivalent) sent to a payee account the customer has never paid before to be held in the bank's Suspense account so that I can review and either release or reject them to prevent fraud.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] When a customer initiates a payment whose EUR-equivalent principal amount (rounded using Math.Round(x, 2, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero)) is >= 5000.00 EUR and the payer customer has no prior completed payment to the destination account, PaymentService places the payment in Held status instead of crediting the payee immediately.
- [ ] When a payment is held, PaymentService transfers (amount + fee) in the payment currency from the payer's account to BankAccounts.For(BankAccountKind.Suspense, currency) via ILedger.PostTransferAsync, notifies the customer via the injected INotifier (injected after IFeeCalculator) without PII, and publishes PaymentHeld(PaymentId, CustomerId, Amount, Currency, clock.UtcNow) via IEventBus.
- [ ] Payments below 5000.00 EUR equivalent, or payments to an account the customer has previously paid, continue to settle immediately without entering Held status.
- [ ] GET api/payments/held, POST api/payments/{id}/release, and POST api/payments/{id}/reject are protected by [Authorize(Policy = Policies.Compliance)] and delegate to IPaymentReviewService.
- [ ] IPaymentReviewService.HeldAsync returns all payments currently in Held status.
- [ ] IPaymentReviewService.ReleaseAsync(paymentId) throws UnauthorizedAccessException if the current user (ICurrentUser.UserId) is the payment's customer or does not hold the Compliance role, throws InvalidOperationException if the payment is not in Held status, and throws an appropriate not-found exception if the payment does not exist.
- [ ] On valid release, ReleaseAsync transfers the payment amount from BankAccounts.For(BankAccountKind.Suspense, currency) to the payee's account and transfers any non-zero fee to BankAccounts.For(BankAccountKind.FeeIncome, currency) via ILedger.PostTransferAsync, transitions the payment out of Held to its completed state through an entity method, notifies the customer via INotifier without PII, and publishes PaymentReleased(paymentId, user.UserId, clock.UtcNow).
- [ ] IPaymentReviewService.RejectAsync(paymentId, reason) enforces the same Compliance role, non-self-decision (UnauthorizedAccessException), and Held-status (InvalidOperationException) guards, requires a non-empty rejection reason, transfers (amount + fee) from BankAccounts.For(BankAccountKind.Suspense, currency) back to the payer's account via ILedger.PostTransferAsync, transitions the payment to Rejected via an entity method, notifies the customer via INotifier without PII, and publishes PaymentRejected(paymentId, user.UserId, clock.UtcNow).
- [ ] All monetary calculations use decimal rounded to 2 decimal places with MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero, all timestamps use IClock.UtcNow, and Payment owns its status via a private setter modified only through domain methods.

## Out of scope
- Making the 5,000 EUR threshold configurable per customer or via admin endpoints.
- Customer-managed trusted payee allowlists or pre-approving new payees.
- Automatic expiry or auto-rejection of Held payments after a time limit.
- Four-eyes approval requiring multiple compliance officers to release a single payment.
- Partial release or partial refund

